      {
        "id": "p9-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "How many subsets did each set have? What pattern do those numbers form?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "(i) 8; (ii) 4; (iii) 2. These are powers of 2: a set with $n$ elements has $2^n$ subsets.",
          "worked": "The lists contain 8, 4 and 2 subsets respectively. In the printed order, the count halves whenever one element is removed. In increasing order of set size, it doubles whenever one element is added:\n\n$2^1=2$, $2^2=4$, $2^3=8$.\n\nEach element can either belong to a subset or be left out, giving $2^n$ subsets for a set with $n$ elements.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
